<%#
# Page header

The header of a super admin page that is not drawn by Administrate: the title,
an optional line under it and the actions on the right (they drop under the
title on a narrow screen). It is the same markup as the headers of the index,
show and form templates, so every page starts alike.

Render it with a block for the actions (an empty block when there are none):
`render layout: 'super_admin/shared/page_header', locals: { title:, description: } do ... end`.

## Local variables:

- `title`: the page title (the `<h1>`).
- `description`: a line under the title (optional).
%>
<% actions = yield %>
<header class="main-content__header" role="banner">
  <div class="main-content__heading">
    <h1 class="main-content__page-title" id="page-title"><%= title %></h1>
    <% if local_assigns[:description].present? %>
      <p class="main-content__description"><%= description %></p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <% if actions.present? %>
    <div class="main-content__actions"><%= actions %></div>
  <% end %>
</header>
